{\label{main}}
For all integers $t > 0$, there exists a $d_0(t)$ such that if $T$ is a $t + 1$-vertex tree and $G$ is an $n$-vertex graph with average degree $d \geq d_0(t)$, then
\begin{equation} {\label{mainbound}}
	|\mathrm{Inj}(T, G)| \geq n d(d - 1) \cdots (d - t + 1).
\end{equation}
If $T$ has diameter at least 3, then equality holds iff $G$ is the disjoint union of cliques of size $d + 1$.

